# This repository holds the tools and nothing else. What follows blocks shapes that would be an
# incident the moment they appeared — not because anyone expects them to, but because **nothing
# else would stop them** if they did.
#
# ~/.claude holds 2.8 GB of transcripts (including real medical records from rounds of
# customer-corpus analysis), every prompt you have ever typed, and snapshots of edited files.
# This repository is deliberately not under there, so in the normal case none of it can arrive;
# this is the second line, for a mistyped cp or a mistaken symlink.
*.jsonl
history*
projects/
file-history/
shell-snapshots/
sessions/
paste-cache/
image-cache/
*.log

# Your registry. It holds the absolute path of every project on your machine and often the
# health endpoints of things you run — it is yours, it is seeded from the example by install.sh,
# and it must never arrive here by accident.
project-icons.json

# originals kept aside during install
*.pre-symlink

__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# serena's index and its notes about this checkout, written by whichever agent is working here.
# Not ignored until 2026-08-19, and `memories/` is the sort of place a project's real names end
# up without anyone deciding they should.
.serena/
